<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">A LITTLE GUIDANCE GOES A LONG WAY</div><h1>Your workshop guide</h1><p>From your first customer to your next completed job.</p></div><button class="btn" data-action="print">Print guide</button></div><section class="panel"><article class="help-content"><h2>1. Make the workspace yours</h2><p>As an administrator, open <a href="/settings">Business settings</a> to change your name, logo, contact details, currency, tax and invoice footer. Choose your currency before creating any work orders. Upload a PNG, JPEG or WebP logo up to 2 MB. Tax changes affect new work orders. Issued invoices retain their original business details.</p><h2>2. Build your workshop directory</h2><ol><li>Add staff in Team & access. Each person gets their own account and role.</li><li>Add suppliers, then parts in Parts & inventory. Use Edit / stock to receive opening stock with a reference.</li><li>Create common labor services and prices in Service catalog.</li><li>Add a customer, then register their vehicle with plate, make, model, year and odometer.</li></ol><h2>3. Schedule a visit</h2><p>Open Appointments and add the vehicle, requested service, start/end time and optional technician. The system checks for overlapping bookings for the same technician. Update the status when the vehicle arrives, the visit is completed, or the customer cancels. Appointments do not automatically create work orders.</p><h2>4. Run a repair from start to finish</h2><ol><li>Create a work order. Select the vehicle, technician, priority, odometer and target completion date. Describe the customer’s concern.</li><li>Add catalog labor, inventory parts, or custom labor lines to the estimate. Quantities are whole units; to bill partial labor time, use a custom line with the final labor price.</li><li>Obtain approval from the customer outside the app. Enter the authorizing customer’s name and record approval. Prices become locked.</li><li>Start repairs. Parts are deducted atomically from stock. If stock is insufficient, receive the missing parts and try again.</li><li>Record diagnosis and inspection findings, then mark the job completed.</li><li>A manager, administrator or cashier issues the invoice from the completed order and sets a payment due date.</li><li>Record payments received by cash, transfer, external card terminal or e-wallet. Partial payments are supported. Print the invoice and payment history or save them as PDF using your browser.</li></ol><p>Cancel an estimate or approved job before repairs start. Work already in progress cannot be cancelled through the MVP. Approved prices and issued invoices cannot be edited. Refunds, credit notes and post-start scope changes require an external accounting process in this release; do not enter negative payments or silently rewrite history.</p><h2>5. Understand staff roles</h2><ul><li><strong>Administrator:</strong> all modules, business settings and staff accounts.</li><li><strong>Manager:</strong> workshop operations, billing, reports, stock, suppliers and activity log.</li><li><strong>Service advisor:</strong> customers, vehicles, appointments, estimates and repair progress; read-only service catalog, stock and invoices.</li><li><strong>Technician:</strong> assigned work orders and their inspection/progress updates; read-only vehicle directory, service catalog and stock.</li><li><strong>Cashier:</strong> invoices, payments and reports; read-only customer, vehicle and work order details.</li></ul><h2>6. Track stock and business health</h2><p>Inventory watch highlights parts at or below their reorder levels. Every stock change is recorded in Stock history. Reports show collections and invoices for a chosen date range; receivables, overdue balances and inventory value are current totals. Export payments to CSV for reconciliation.</p><h2>7. Common issues</h2><ul><li><strong>Incorrect login:</strong> check the email and password. After repeated attempts, wait for the cooldown. Ask an administrator to reset your password if needed.</li><li><strong>Access denied:</strong> your role does not have that permission, or the job is assigned to another technician.</li><li><strong>Record cannot be deleted:</strong> linked service, payment or stock history is protected.</li><li><strong>Logo does not appear:</strong> the server administrator should run <code>php artisan storage:link</code> and check storage permissions.</li><li><strong>Expired page:</strong> reload the form and sign in again if necessary.</li></ul><h2>Account security</h2><p>Click your account name in the sidebar to change your password. Temporary passwords must be replaced at first login. Never share accounts. Administrators can deactivate staff immediately. Technical setup, database backup, deployment, security and route documentation are in the project’s <code>docs/</code> directory.</p></article></section>
